startup.source.run_user:
Starts when you sign in to Windows. Switching it OFF stops it from starting, but it stays installed and you can switch it back ON.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}
• Source · your account

startup.source.run_machine:
Starts when any user signs in to Windows. Switching it OFF stops it from starting, but it stays installed and you can switch it back ON.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}
• Source · all users

startup.source.folder_user:
Starts from your Startup folder. Switching it OFF stops it from starting, but the shortcut stays and you can switch it back ON.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}
• Source · your Startup folder

startup.source.folder_machine:
Starts from the Startup folder of all users. Switching it OFF stops it from starting, but the shortcut stays and you can switch it back ON.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}
• Source · all users' Startup folder

startup.source.service:
A background service that starts with Windows. Task Manager does not list it in Startup. Switching it OFF sets it to Manual, so it stops starting by itself but can still be started when something needs it. Security, VPN and database services may stop working properly. Only available with Safe mode OFF.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}

startup.source.service_updater:
An updater service that starts with Windows. Switching it OFF sets it to Manual, so it stops starting by itself but can still run when something needs it. Updates for that software may arrive later.
• Name · {name}
• Command · {command}
